  "description": "32-bit ARM Cortex-M3 microcontroller in LQFP-48 with 64 KB flash, 20 KB SRAM and a 72 MHz max clock. It packs USB 2.0 full-speed, CAN, dual 12-bit ADCs, multiple timers, SPI/I2C/USART and DMA, vastly more capable than 8-bit AVRs at a similar low price. Famous as the heart of the ultra-cheap 'Blue Pill' board, popular for learning ARM, robotics and USB projects. Standout value: full Cortex-M3 performance with USB for a couple of dollars.",
