  "typical_application": "Low-cost 32-bit projects needing USB, CAN, or fast ADC/PWM such as robotics controllers, USB peripherals, and CNC/3D-printer boards.",
  "gotchas": [
    "3.3 V only; the GPIO are not 5 V tolerant except the few marked FT pins, so naive 5 V wiring can damage the chip",
    "Blue Pill clones use a wrong USB D+ pull-up resistor (often 10k instead of 1.5k), so USB enumeration is unreliable until the resistor is changed or PA12 is briefly pulled low",
    "many boards ship with cloned or remarked dies (e.g. CKS/CS32 CH32) that misbehave with the official ST USB DFU bootloader",
    "BOOT0 (pin 44) and BOOT1/PB2 (pin 20) jumpers must be set correctly to enter the serial/system bootloader",
    "PA13/PA14 are SWDIO/SWCLK; configuring them as plain GPIO disables SWD debugging and can lock you out without a boot-mode recovery",
    "datasheet 64 KB flash is often physically 128 KB but unguaranteed; relying on the extra is non-portable"
  ],
